item.text:
Buhari’s 2022 Chapter 1B exposure is limited and mostly civil-nuclear, not weaponized. The record I found supports: formal nonproliferation constraints, a domestic safeguards/regulatory apparatus, and some 2022 nuclear-program capacity building. I did not find evidence of nuclear brinkmanship, command-and-control decisions over nuclear forces, or other material existential-risk choices attributable to Buhari in 2022. That is an inference from the source set, not a score.

Reused evidence: none.

New evidence:
